==Old Norse==

===Etymology 1===
From {{proto|Germanic|hleuzan|cheek, ear|lang=non}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|k'leus-|temple of the forehead, cheek|lang=non}}. More at {{l|en|leer}}.

====Noun====
{{infl|non|noun|g=n|sort=hlyr}}

# [[cheek]]; [[face]]
# The sides (cheeks) of an [[axe]] blade, [[knife]], or [[bodice]]

===Etymology 2===
From {{proto|Germanic|hliwjaz||hlēwaz||hlēwiaz|warm|lang=non}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|k'al(w)e-||k'el(w)e-||k(')lēw-|warm, hot|lang=non}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|hleow|hlēow|warm, sunny|lang=ang}}. More at {{l|en|lukewarm}}. 

====Adjective====
{{non-adj}}

# [[warm]], [[mild]]

